WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.674
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.675 --> 00:03.343
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION AND
SHAMEFUL ACTS ARE NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:03.344 --> 00:04.970
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:47.388 --> 00:49.598
The sea really is amazing!

00:50.349 --> 00:51.933
Iori-kun.

00:51.934 --> 00:52.560
Huh?

00:53.394 --> 00:54.645
I have a letter for you.

00:55.437 --> 00:56.981
It's from Shiori-chan.

00:57.606 --> 00:58.816
Shiori?

01:05.364 --> 01:08.992
<i>Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth</i>

01:08.993 --> 01:11.996
<i>Right now is always
the best of the season</i>

01:12.204 --> 01:15.665
<i>Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning</i>

01:15.666 --> 01:19.210
<i>Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world</i>

01:19.211 --> 01:22.463
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

01:22.464 --> 01:24.633
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:25.843 --> 01:27.511
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:29.263 --> 01:30.806
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:32.683 --> 01:34.059
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:34.727 --> 01:39.522
<i>Mon-Tues-Weds-Thurs-Fri,
my life knows no variety</i>

01:39.523 --> 01:40.941
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:41.358 --> 01:46.154
Sat-Sun, wake up in the afternoon
with only my smartphone to surf

01:46.155 --> 01:47.739
<i>Ever Endless</i>

01:47.740 --> 01:49.157
<i>All my limbs' been giving in</i>

01:49.158 --> 01:50.992
<i>Kalbi's a burden
like my lumber spine</i>

01:50.993 --> 01:52.577
<i>Doing family
service with irises dim</i>

01:52.578 --> 01:54.205
<i>But you know that
I'll go all the way</i>

01:54.622 --> 01:57.791
<i>Glitter, shimmer,
the light's shining</i>

01:58.042 --> 02:01.628
Let's give it one more chance

02:01.629 --> 02:05.090
<i>Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth</i>

02:05.299 --> 02:08.093
<i>Right now is always
the best of the season</i>

02:08.302 --> 02:11.930
<i>Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning</i>

02:11.931 --> 02:14.934
<i>Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world</i>

02:15.142 --> 02:17.310
<i>Youth is when you never...</i>

02:17.311 --> 02:18.811
<i>stop chasing your own values</i>

02:18.812 --> 02:20.480
<i>Our youth's eternal</i>

02:20.481 --> 02:22.065
<i>the color never fades with age</i>

02:22.066 --> 02:23.942
<i>Youth is when you keep...</i>

02:23.943 --> 02:25.485
<i>getting lost along the way</i>

02:25.486 --> 02:28.989
<i>Youth is Forever</i>

02:30.824 --> 02:32.576
<i>Dear Big Brother.</i>

02:32.826 --> 02:36.205
<i>Are you doing well amidst
the thriving greenery?</i>

02:36.539 --> 02:39.415
<i>At home, the flowers
are in full bloom</i>

02:39.416 --> 02:41.919
<i>and they cover the mountain
in summer's shadings.</i>

02:42.795 --> 02:45.756
<i>It has been three months
since you left for college.</i>

02:46.048 --> 02:48.299
<i>Have you been causing trouble</i>

02:48.300 --> 02:51.637
<i>for Big Sister Nanaka and
Chisa as well as our own uncle?</i>

02:52.388 --> 02:55.349
<i>Have you been devoting
yourself earnestly to your study?</i>

02:55.808 --> 02:57.518
<i>I'm very worried.</i>

02:57.935 --> 03:00.729
<i>Mom and Dad are also
very worried about you.</i>

03:01.438 --> 03:05.108
<i>I wish that you could come home,
but if that is too much to ask for,</i>

03:05.109 --> 03:07.486
<i>please let me know
what you've been up to.</i>

03:07.987 --> 03:11.156
<i>I'm looking forward
to your response.</i>

03:11.740 --> 03:12.616
<i>Sincerely.</i>

03:13.868 --> 03:18.038
<i>P.S. I had some leftover
fabric, so I tried making a doll.</i>

03:18.747 --> 03:22.251
<i>I would be happy if you kept it
and thought of it as if it were myself.</i>

03:23.127 --> 03:24.169
Iori-kun.

03:25.129 --> 03:27.464
Have you written a
reply to Shiori-chan?

03:27.715 --> 03:28.799
Nanaka-san.

03:29.383 --> 03:32.969
Actually, I'm not planning
to write back right now.

03:32.970 --> 03:34.679
Oh, why is that?

03:34.680 --> 03:37.766
They say no news is
good news, after all.

03:38.267 --> 03:39.977
Well, that's true.

03:40.728 --> 03:44.440
Then, how about I write to her
about how you've been doing instead?

03:44.773 --> 03:46.025
You would do that?

03:46.192 --> 03:46.775
Yeah.

03:47.193 --> 03:50.404
Both Chisa-chan and I
have received letters as well.

03:50.988 --> 03:53.323
Besides, it's only natural...

03:53.324 --> 03:55.409
for family members
to stick together.

03:56.368 --> 03:57.620
You want to bet on that?

03:57.786 --> 03:59.455
As I report my situation...

04:00.164 --> 04:03.125
Don't, do anything
else but that!

04:03.626 --> 04:07.254
However, it seems that Chisa-chan
has already started writing.

04:07.546 --> 04:09.756
Wait, don't you dare
write anything down!

04:09.757 --> 04:10.673
Why?

04:10.674 --> 04:13.134
I'll write down what's
been going on with me later.

04:13.135 --> 04:15.304
You just write
about yourself, deal?

04:15.429 --> 04:18.057
I don't mind, but
Shiori-chan said...

04:18.307 --> 04:22.228
"Please let me know if big
brother is lying to me in reality."

04:22.436 --> 04:23.437
Tch...

04:23.771 --> 04:25.647
So let me know
when you're finished.

04:25.648 --> 04:27.065
I need to check it through.

04:27.066 --> 04:28.651
Sure, I'll get it done.

04:28.817 --> 04:31.654
<i>Shit. Now I'm in the
purgatory of my own making.</i>

04:31.904 --> 04:35.658
<i>On top of living together, Chisa is in
the same club and the same degree.</i>

04:36.116 --> 04:38.827
<i>She knows every waking
detail about my daily life.</i>

04:39.286 --> 04:40.996
<i>Lying is not an option.</i>

04:41.664 --> 04:45.000
<i>In that case, my one option is to
write the best I can no matter what.</i>

04:46.085 --> 04:47.836
<i>To Shiori.</i>

04:48.504 --> 04:50.506
<i>It's almost summer here too.</i>

04:54.718 --> 04:55.594
<i>With love, Iori.</i>

04:56.095 --> 04:57.220
Where's the main part?

04:57.221 --> 05:00.099
There's not a single
thing that I can write about.

05:00.474 --> 05:02.434
Let me do it then, you dingus.

05:02.768 --> 05:03.977
No, it's all right.

05:03.978 --> 05:06.814
I just couldn't think of a
way to start the letter off.

05:06.939 --> 05:08.065
Oh...

05:08.566 --> 05:11.109
If that's the case, how
about an "opening formula?"

05:11.110 --> 05:12.570
Hmm, I see.

05:14.446 --> 05:15.406
<i>Opening formula.</i>

05:16.824 --> 05:17.700
<i>Middle formula.</i>

05:19.493 --> 05:20.244
<i>Closing formula.</i>

05:20.578 --> 05:20.785
You-

05:20.786 --> 05:22.955
Please give me
one more chance...

05:23.289 --> 05:26.458
Maybe it'd be easier if I
give him some topics instead?

05:26.667 --> 05:28.793
Then write about
your club activities,

05:28.794 --> 05:31.796
your studies, and
your personal life.

05:31.797 --> 05:34.967
Okay, I will write a letter
free of lies and fiction.

05:35.217 --> 05:37.177
CLUB ACTIVITIES

05:37.178 --> 05:38.345
<i>Dear Shiori.</i>

05:38.804 --> 05:42.474
<i>I'm currently in a diving
club that is called Peek a Boo.</i>

05:43.267 --> 05:45.644
<i>Every member here is
a gentleman of virtue.</i>

05:46.937 --> 05:49.105
<i>- Rock-Paper-Stripper!
- Rock-Paper-Stripper!</i>

05:49.106 --> 05:50.607
<i>What is this?</i>

05:50.608 --> 05:51.816
<i>They taught me...</i>

05:51.817 --> 05:54.069
<i>- how to express who I truly am.
- Wait a minute!</i>

05:56.197 --> 05:58.157
STUDIES

05:58.407 --> 05:59.949
<i>It took me by surprise</i>

05:59.950 --> 06:03.454
<i>how incredibly different university
is from middle and high school.</i>

06:04.205 --> 06:06.207
<i>The tests are difficult,</i>

06:06.540 --> 06:09.919
<i>but everyone works hard
and are fully prepared for it.</i>

06:10.461 --> 06:12.630
<i>Kitahara, are you
cheating again?</i>

06:12.838 --> 06:14.798
<i>So, how do we sneak this in?</i>

06:15.090 --> 06:16.382
<i>Within the pencil case.</i>

06:16.383 --> 06:17.383
PLAN 1 WITHIN THE PENCIL CASE

06:17.384 --> 06:19.135
<i>On the drink label.</i>

06:19.136 --> 06:19.887
PLAN 2 DRINK LABEL

06:20.095 --> 06:21.596
<i>Inside the towel.</i>

06:21.597 --> 06:22.348
PLAN 3 INSIDE THE TOWEL

06:22.765 --> 06:23.848
<i>I'll stick it on my arm.</i>

06:23.849 --> 06:24.974
HIS ARM <i>I'll stick it on my arm.</i>

06:24.975 --> 06:26.726
We must never
give up until the end.

06:26.727 --> 06:28.937
Let's get our credits together.

06:28.938 --> 06:30.855
<i>- Right!
- Right!</i>

06:30.856 --> 06:32.816
PERSONAL LIFE

06:32.983 --> 06:36.487
<i>As for my personal life, I cannot
think of anything to write of.</i>

06:37.154 --> 06:39.697
<i>I live a self-disciplined
life every day.</i>

06:39.698 --> 06:41.115
<i>Damn it!</i>

06:41.116 --> 06:43.576
<i>We're exactly one
hour late again.</i>

06:43.577 --> 06:45.204
<i>Do you think we'll
make a roll call?</i>

06:45.496 --> 06:47.665
<i>I did not wear any
dirty clothes either.</i>

06:48.123 --> 06:50.583
<i>Have some damn dignity
and wear pants for once!</i>

06:50.584 --> 06:53.504
<i>And some days have left
me inspired and motivated.</i>

06:54.088 --> 06:55.965
BREAK UP WITH CHISA
KOTEGAWA OR GO TO HELL

06:57.508 --> 06:59.175
<i>That's not what it was!</i>

06:59.176 --> 07:00.593
<i>No, what I meant was...</i>

07:00.594 --> 07:01.719
<i>I get it, I get it.</i>

07:01.720 --> 07:03.596
<i>Tell us more
behind the mountain.</i>

07:03.597 --> 07:05.099
<i>You didn't bother to listen!</i>

07:05.266 --> 07:07.226
<i>I'm doing well so
there's no need to worry.</i>

07:07.893 --> 07:10.604
<i>Please send my best
regards to mother and father.</i>

07:11.647 --> 07:12.857
I see.

07:13.440 --> 07:15.401
Is that so, Big Brother?

07:17.027 --> 07:20.281
But receiving letters these
days must have been really nice.

07:20.739 --> 07:22.366
And it's not a
text or something.

07:22.491 --> 07:24.994
No, that's not it.

07:25.244 --> 07:28.496
That girl cannot comprehend
technology whatsoever.

07:28.497 --> 07:29.539
Oh my.

07:29.540 --> 07:31.583
Let alone a PC or a smartphone,

07:31.584 --> 07:34.128
she probably can't
even use a rice cooker.

07:34.295 --> 07:35.504
Is that so?

07:35.671 --> 07:38.048
Everyone has something
they're not good at.

07:38.257 --> 07:41.635
Well I was able to get away
with it thanks to that fact this time.

07:41.886 --> 07:44.138
Even though it's
far from the truth.

07:44.555 --> 07:46.849
Actually, I
technically didn't lie.

07:47.141 --> 07:49.809
Okay, if you've learned your
lesson, then from now on...

07:49.810 --> 07:50.769
That's true.

07:50.978 --> 07:52.104
So from now on,

07:52.897 --> 07:54.815
I can finally go
out with the boys!

07:57.151 --> 07:59.987
- Let's go!
- Cheers!

08:00.321 --> 08:01.530
You're the worst.

08:04.783 --> 08:06.327
Oh dear.

08:07.077 --> 08:10.664
A big brother who lies
requires more close monitoring.

08:11.290 --> 08:12.541
Isn't that right?

08:16.879 --> 08:18.130
Good evening.

08:19.215 --> 08:20.758
What's up with you two?

08:21.258 --> 08:21.966
Huh?

08:21.967 --> 08:23.676
Isn't there a meeting today?

08:23.677 --> 08:24.802
Come on now.

08:24.803 --> 08:26.430
That's next week.

08:26.639 --> 08:27.180
Ah!

08:27.181 --> 08:28.223
Seriously?

08:28.224 --> 08:30.225
No wonder no one's here.

08:30.226 --> 08:32.520
They talked about
it at the last meeting.

08:32.811 --> 08:34.939
I completely forgot.

08:35.397 --> 08:37.148
Where's Nanaka-san
and the manager?

08:37.149 --> 08:38.526
They're on a business trip.

08:41.237 --> 08:42.654
Alrighty.

08:42.655 --> 08:43.948
Shall we start?

08:44.156 --> 08:45.491
What are you on about?

08:46.116 --> 08:47.117
Dinner.

08:51.747 --> 08:52.706
Thanks.

08:56.585 --> 08:58.379
What's wrong, Cakey?

08:59.129 --> 09:00.089
Nothing.

09:00.339 --> 09:02.007
Let me have a taste.

09:02.216 --> 09:02.925
Okay.

09:04.051 --> 09:05.426
Isn't it a bit spicy?

09:05.427 --> 09:06.595
Is that so?

09:07.429 --> 09:08.639
I'm gonna go help.

09:11.725 --> 09:13.768
I'll be the one to
make dessert then.

09:13.769 --> 09:14.520
Huh?

09:14.854 --> 09:15.895
There's no need to...

09:15.896 --> 09:17.064
It's fine.

09:17.356 --> 09:19.315
What's going on with her?

09:19.316 --> 09:21.025
Did something happen?

09:21.026 --> 09:22.819
Cakey kicked me out.

09:22.820 --> 09:23.654
I see.

09:24.196 --> 09:25.447
So, what do you think?

09:25.739 --> 09:26.656
About what?

09:26.657 --> 09:28.700
- Ah! Ouch!
- Aina?

09:28.701 --> 09:31.035
You think she'll make
something decent?

09:31.036 --> 09:33.163
Probably a 60/40 chance.

09:33.706 --> 09:35.541
- Thanks for the food.
- Thanks for the food.

09:36.041 --> 09:38.335
So you settled for some
fruits in the end, eh?

09:38.544 --> 09:40.671
What were you
trying to make at first?

09:41.297 --> 09:42.047
Pudding.

09:42.506 --> 09:45.217
I know an easy recipe
to help you with next time.

09:45.467 --> 09:46.635
By the way.

09:46.844 --> 09:47.428
Hmm?

09:47.678 --> 09:49.930
Are you two often home alone?

09:50.598 --> 09:53.558
Sometimes, maybe once a month.

09:53.559 --> 09:55.186
Is that okay?

09:55.311 --> 09:56.436
What do you mean "okay?"

09:56.437 --> 09:57.645
What's okay?

09:57.646 --> 09:59.607
Ah, no, I mean...

10:00.024 --> 10:03.444
I wonder if any "incidents"
might have happened lately.

10:04.111 --> 10:05.196
- Huh?
- Huh?

10:05.529 --> 10:07.447
What do you mean "incidents?"

10:07.448 --> 10:09.241
What are you talking about?

10:09.617 --> 10:14.037
Well... you once said
that Chisa has a nice butt.

10:14.038 --> 10:15.748
You did say that.

10:15.956 --> 10:19.668
And to be pretty honest, she
does have a big and nice butt.

10:19.835 --> 10:20.920
Aina?!

10:21.086 --> 10:23.130
Well, what do you have to say?

10:23.339 --> 10:24.840
Let's see.

10:25.090 --> 10:27.718
It's true she has
a very nice butt.

10:28.219 --> 10:30.304
But she's like a sister to me.

10:30.638 --> 10:32.764
O-Oh, is that so?

10:32.765 --> 10:33.807
I see.

10:35.226 --> 10:37.810
So are you saying that you
are ready to make a move?

10:37.811 --> 10:38.937
Wait a minute.

10:38.938 --> 10:40.980
What would you do
with a "little sister"?

10:40.981 --> 10:43.317
Don't make me say it.
They're embarassing.

10:43.609 --> 10:46.028
What are you planning to
do that can't be said out loud?

10:46.320 --> 10:49.240
The only embarrassing thing
here are your own thoughts!

10:49.490 --> 10:52.367
Seriously, this is
why 2D-Brain is crap.

10:52.368 --> 10:55.079
I really don't know
what you're thinking.

10:55.204 --> 10:56.497
That's true.

10:57.039 --> 11:00.668
The truth is, no one would feel
that way about their little sister.

11:00.876 --> 11:02.127
Isn't that true?

11:05.965 --> 11:09.425
That's right. No one would feel
that way about their little sister.

11:09.426 --> 11:11.136
Why is everyone looking away?

11:11.720 --> 11:15.891
People without little
sisters always say that.

11:16.225 --> 11:18.893
But they're not as
great as you'd think.

11:18.894 --> 11:20.771
Iori has a little sister?

11:21.021 --> 11:23.357
Huh? Well, sort of.

11:23.607 --> 11:25.066
Wait, Kitahara.

11:25.067 --> 11:25.776
Huh?

11:25.901 --> 11:27.570
Before you answer...

11:30.197 --> 11:32.408
Be wary of the words
you will say soon.

11:34.159 --> 11:34.993
I don't have one.

11:34.994 --> 11:36.996
Look me in the eye and say it.

11:37.204 --> 11:39.456
Her name is Shiori-chan
and she's adorable.

11:40.457 --> 11:41.666
O-One...

11:41.667 --> 11:43.543
Hey wait, what are you counting?

11:43.544 --> 11:44.377
How old is she?

11:44.378 --> 11:46.797
I think she's in her third
year of middle school.

11:47.089 --> 11:48.172
T-Two...

11:48.173 --> 11:50.426
Stop it, that counting
is weirding me out!

11:50.801 --> 11:52.428
Does she get along with Iori?

11:52.887 --> 11:56.140
I feel like she's still a
bit too attached to him.

11:56.348 --> 11:58.349
Th-Th-Three!!

11:58.350 --> 11:59.350
This is disturbing.

11:59.351 --> 12:01.937
I think he's been possessed
by a monstrous spirit!

12:02.354 --> 12:04.940
She sent me a
letter the other day.

12:05.441 --> 12:08.776
Oh, getting a letter rather
than a text must be nice.

12:08.777 --> 12:09.527
Yeah.

12:09.528 --> 12:12.656
Probably since she doesn't
know how to use a smartphone.

12:12.865 --> 12:13.866
Is that so?

12:14.074 --> 12:16.202
She's terrible with technology.

12:16.368 --> 12:19.330
Maybe she's just acting
dumb in front of you?

12:19.914 --> 12:23.417
And whether we sent out a reply,
we got even more letters back

12:23.834 --> 12:25.586
along with this.

12:25.920 --> 12:27.545
She said she made it herself.

12:27.546 --> 12:28.797
Ah, so cute.

12:28.964 --> 12:32.051
I was thinking of sending
her some photos in return.

12:32.218 --> 12:33.426
You can't do that.

12:33.427 --> 12:34.386
Why not?

12:34.595 --> 12:37.556
If my lifestyle gets out,
so goes my allowance.

12:37.681 --> 12:40.267
If you're aware of what will
happen, change your ways.

12:40.476 --> 12:43.479
If you insist, we can
pick out some to send.

12:43.729 --> 12:44.687
Fine then.

12:44.688 --> 12:45.898
Useless big brother.

12:48.609 --> 12:51.736
I can't find any photos to send
other than underwater ones.

12:51.737 --> 12:53.948
It's because you're
always naked.

12:54.114 --> 12:56.867
You're more exposed
on land than in the sea.

12:57.117 --> 12:59.370
The pictures of people
sleeping are funny...

13:00.788 --> 13:01.996
Chisa, Chisa.

13:01.997 --> 13:02.831
What?

13:03.082 --> 13:03.749
Look.

13:04.416 --> 13:06.377
Huh? What about that photo?

13:06.877 --> 13:08.294
It's nothing.

13:08.295 --> 13:09.421
Don't worry about it.

13:10.047 --> 13:12.423
The breasts were spilling out.

13:12.424 --> 13:15.427
Both Big Sis and
Azusa-san <i>are</i> big after all.

13:16.637 --> 13:17.388
I see.

13:18.848 --> 13:22.351
So it has to be a precious photo
of Nanaka-san and Azusa-san.

13:22.685 --> 13:24.769
W-We can't show it to you.

13:24.770 --> 13:27.189
I need to erase the file too.

13:27.648 --> 13:29.567
I won't ask you to show me.

13:29.984 --> 13:30.609
Huh?

13:31.235 --> 13:32.735
Is that so?

13:32.736 --> 13:34.446
If that's the case,
then it's fine.

13:35.990 --> 13:37.199
I'm going to the restroom.

13:37.366 --> 13:38.284
Okay.

13:40.327 --> 13:41.537
<i>I am in dire need...</i>

13:41.871 --> 13:45.040
<i>of seeing it!</i>

13:46.667 --> 13:49.378
<i>But there's no way
they'd let me if I ask.</i>

